---
title: "Auto-Generate Columns"
enterprise: true
---

When working with dynamic or unknown datasets, manually defining `columnDefs` can be impractical. The Auto-Generate Columns feature allows the grid to create column definitions automatically from the provided row data.

## Enabling Auto-Generate Columns

Set `autoGenerateColumnDefs` to `true` to enable automatic column generation. The grid will extract keys from the first row of `rowData` and create a `ColDef` for each key.

```js
const gridOptions = {
    autoGenerateColumnDefs: true,
    rowData: [
        { name: 'Alice', age: 30, country: 'US' },
        { name: 'Bob', age: 25, country: 'UK' },
    ],
};
```

This produces the equivalent of:

```js
columnDefs: [
    { field: 'name' },
    { field: 'age' },
    { field: 'country' },
]
```

Columns are regenerated each time `rowData` is updated. Column IDs are derived from the `field` value, so matching columns update in place when data changes.

## Customising Generated Columns

Use the `processAutoGeneratedColumnDefs` callback to modify, reorder, or replace the generated columns before they are applied.

```js
const gridOptions = {
    autoGenerateColumnDefs: true,
    processAutoGeneratedColumnDefs: (params) => {
        return params.colDefs.map((colDef) => ({
            ...colDef,
            sortable: true,
            filter: true,
        }));
    },
};
```

The callback receives:

- `params.colDefs` — the auto-generated column definitions
- `params.rowData` — the raw row data used for generation

The returned array is used as the final `columnDefs`.

## Clearing Data

Setting `rowData` to `[]` or `null` clears row data only — column definitions are preserved. To reset columns, clear them explicitly:

```js
api.setGridOption('columnDefs', []);
```

